<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Tiberina Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1798 CE – 1798 CE · capital Perugia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived republic proclaimed in Perugia in 1798, quickly absorbed into the French-backed Roman Republic.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In February 1798, as French troops overthrew papal rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, patriots in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-perugia">Perugia</a> and the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiber-river">Tiber</a> valley proclaimed a republic named after the river, taking over the government of Perugia and nearby Umbrian towns.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known mainly from local records, the Tiberina Republic was a provisional government of local patriots under French protection. It replaced papal officials, planted liberty trees and adopted republican symbols.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Within weeks, in 1798, it was merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/roman-republic-1798-1799">Roman Republic</a> (1798–1799), and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-perugia">Perugia</a> became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> capital of that state.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1798 CE – 1798 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.48%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1798 CE – 1798 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Perugia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Repubblica Tiberina</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=tiberina-republic" aria-label="Tiberina Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4979 647 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tiberina Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5299 903L5304 942M5299 903L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5299 903h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5299 903h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1798&amp;focus=tiberina-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
